 {
  "doc_id": "d418",
  "date": "1941-12-06",
  "title": "President Roosevelt to Emperor Hirohito of Japan  This message was transmitted in telegram No. 818, December 6, 1941, 9 p.m., to the Ambassador in Japan (Grew), with instructions to communicate the President’s message, to the Japanese, Emperor in such manner as deemed most appropriate by the Ambassador and at the earliest possible moment, addressed to “His Imperial Majesty, the Emperor of Japan.” The telegram added that the press was being informed that the President was despatching a message to the Emperor.",
